 her rebellious  Nature by sticking it to a nearby pole  badass after a while Veronica's parents  depart and Heather escorts her to their  room it is a dark and gloomy looking  room which consists of only two beds a  table and an alarm clock as Veronica is  unpacking Heather politely offers to  help but gets declined Veronica then  chastises her for ratting her out  earlier she also asks Heather to cut the  act as their creepy principle is not  here anymore however to her surprise  Heather mentions that she is just  following the rules and that she will  continue doing so until they are inside  the school premises weirded out by her  behavior Veronica aims to relax by  listening to some music on her MP3  speaker but even this time Heather  intervenes she quickly turns off the  speaker and warns Veronica that music is  not allowed here before leaving she also  says that Mr Welch will be giving her a  new haircut soon something about that  sounds so gross the next morning  Veronica is woken up sharp at 5am by a  combination of the alarm clock and  Heather still sleepy she gets dressed in  her school uniform and heads to the  canteen where all the girls are enjoying  their breakfast and chattering the  strange thing is that none of them are  shouting and laughing like normal girls  their age would normally do they also  appear to be dull and lethargic almost  as if they are robots meanwhile Veronica  goes to the counter for some food but  learns that they only serve sausage and  bacon oh no this means that she will  have to change her vegan lifestyle from  now on the scene then cuts to the class  where a male history teacher David is  explaining different events from the  past where children disobeyed their  parents and got punished it turns out  that in this school even all the classes  are designed to brainwash the students  to be obedient and polite Veronica finds  the information very false and  interrupts David saying children have  every right to be impolite because their  age makes them immature and carefree  hearing this the entire class becomes  shocked as this is the first time  someone has contradicted their teacher  however David calms them down mentioning  that Veronica will soon become polite  before the class ends he also asks her  why she hasn't gotten her hair cut yet  shortly after Veronica is wandering  around the playground When Miss  Genevieve summons her to her office on  reaching there she notices the barber Mr  Welch waiting for her surprisingly he  starts taking measurements of her head  and even asks her age something which is  definitely not required for a haircut  after noting down all the details Mr  Welch mentions that he won't be able to  book a haircut appointment until at  least the next week as he is totally  busy for the next few days however when  Miss Genevieve insists he cancels one  appointment and Promises to give  Veronica a haircut the following day at  this point Veronica has started to  realize that something is really wrong  with this school they don't even have  iPads so that the teachers don't have to  do their jobs hence at midnight while  her roommate is asleep she packs her  belongings and prepares to escape the  school but as soon as she gets out of  the main door a fellow student named  Claire stops her revealing that it's not  easy to escape the place there are  electric fences surrounding the school  and on the road several guards are  always patrolling following this the two  introduce themselves and Claire takes  Veronica to her room there she shows her  the sketches of two former students who  apparently tried to escape but were  caught they had calculated all the  movements of the guards but despite this  they were still caught they were  probably turned into Piggies too and  made into bacon after the Revelation  Claire tells Veronica that she doesn't  have much time left as her haircut is  scheduled for the next day she claims  that the haircut is what changes the  students into dull robots Veronica is  obviously confused by all this so Claire  decides to show her something she leads  her through a secret tunnel and soon  they reach a room where Miss Genevieve  Mr Welch and another student are present  the student is tied to a chair and she  keeps asking to be released but miss  Genevieve is unfazed all she says is  don't worry my child you will be polite  in no time saying this she orders the  barber Dr Welch to initiate the process  as the tied up student screams in fear  he puts a strange helmet on her head and  starts giving her a haircut after a  while her hairstyle has changed and so  is her behavior the girl who was  rebellious arrogant and rude just a few  minutes ago has now become calm and  polite Veronica who is watching from a  distance with Claire finally understands  how the students are straightened out  here she does that Tech makes no sense  meanwhile Claire reveals that she  fractured her head when she was a child  and the metal plate had to be put inside  her head as a precaution this plate  apparently saved her from turning into  one of those doll students when she got  a haircut last year later as the two  continue talking Claire mentions the  reason why she doesn't want to escape  she and her sister both arrived at the  school on the same day but only she  retained her sanity now if she leaves  alone she fears that Genevieve will harm  her sister hearing all this Veronica  promises to come up with a plan to  release all the students from the spell  that is constricting them the following  morning at the canteen she tries to  encourage the students to be rebellious  by whistling but ends up getting  reprimanded by Miss Genevieve during  their conversation Veronica accidentally  reveals that she and Claire witnessed  the haircut session of a fellow student  this angers Miss Genevieve and she  promises to change Veronica for good in  the evening a few hours later a scared  Veronica rushes to her only friend  Claire's room only to find out that  she's gotten a brand new haircut it  turns out that after Veronica  inadvertently revealed that they were  spying on Mr Welch the other night Miss  Genevieve approached Claire removed the  metal plate from the head and gave her  another haircut now she is emotionless  and dull like all the other students  with this Veronica's Only Hope of  Escaping The Wretched school is gone  feeling sorry for herself instead of  feeling guilty for getting her only  friend lobotomized classic Veronica  later she lies in her bed waiting for  Miss Genevieve to take her away and  change her forever meanwhile her  roommate Heather arrives and mentions  that it's supper time so they should go  however Veronica is in no mood instead  she starts talking about her childhood  days where she used to be happy and  didn't care a bit about what was  happening in the world she then asks  Heather about what it's like to live a  boring and controlled life but as  expected the latter doesn't understand a  word she is saying despite this Veronica  decides to give her roommate a parting  gift she brings out her MP3 speaker and  hands it to Heather who is speechless  throughout the encounter in the  background some static noises can be  heard implying that Heather is trying to  recall her past memories suddenly she  presses a button on the speaker and a  pop song starts playing Heather feels  excruciating pain in her ears but after  a while she calms down surprisingly she  has regained her sanity and all the  memories that she had before the haircut  in fact she doesn't even remember how  she ended up in this school this makes  Veronica very happy as she has finally  found an antidote to cure the six  students holy crap Nicki Minaj is good  for something hence without wasting any  time she starts plotting something with  Heather after a while she goes to miss  Genevieve's office and mentions that she  is ready for the haircut the two then  head towards Mr Welch's barber shop but  along the way Veronica changes her  attitude and starts insulting Miss  Genevieve at the same time she signals  her roommate to initiate their plan  Heather who is actually in Miss  Genevieve's office brings out the MP3  speaker and puts it right next to a  microphone then she turns on the speaker  and the same pop song from earlier  starts blasting from all the  announcement devices in the school at  first all the students are deeply  affected by the music but soon they turn  into their real selves Claire who is in  the canteen finally reconvenes with her  sister after a year in the final scene  all the girls come out on the playground  screaming and having fun like normal  teenagers do miss Genevieve tries to  order them back inside their rooms but  to no avail with the spell now broken  the girls are wild and carefree as they  should be the movie ends as all the  students including Veronica Heather and  Claire run towards the exit gate of the  school probably about to get mowed down  by the guards subscribe for more videos  like this turn on notifications and  leave a like to help the channel out  thank you for watching
 

